ad","Deanne N. Den Hartog"],"y":2018,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Business Ethics","v":"151","i":"3","p":"613-626","r":94,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10551-016-3251-2","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1007/s10551-016-3251-2"},{"t":"How Do Controls Impact Employee Trust in the Employer?","a":["Antoinette Weibel","Deanne N. Den Hartog","Nicole Gillespie","Rosalind Searle","Frédérique Six","Denise Skinner"],"y":2016,"c":"pub","j":"Human Resource Management","v":"55","i":"3","p":"437-462","r":89,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1002/hrm.21733","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1002/hrm.21733"},{"t":"Exploring the Role of Leadership in Enabling Contextual Ambidexterity","a":["Liselore A. Havermans","Deanne N. Den Hartog","Anne Keegan","Mary Uhl‐Bien"],"y":2015,"c":"pub","j":"Human Resource Management","v":"54","i":"S1","r":89,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1002/hrm.21764","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1002/hrm.21764"},{"t":"Leading Machiavellians: How to Translate Machiavellians’ Selfishness Into Pro-Organizational Behavior","a":["Frank D. Belschak","Deanne N. Den Hartog","Karianne Kalshoven"],"y":2015,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Management","v":"41","i":"7","p":"1934-1956","r":102,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0149206313484513","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1177/0149206313484513"},{"t":"(Un)Ethical Behavior and Performance Appraisal: The Role of Affect, Support, and Organizational Justice","a":["Gabriele Jacobs","Frank D. Belschak","Deanne N. Den Hartog"],"y":2013,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Business Ethics","r":94,"n":"Forthcoming","l":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10551-013-1687-1","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1007/s10551-013-1687-1"},{"t":"HRM, Communication, Satisfaction, and Perceived Performance: A Cross-Level Test","a":["Deanne N. Den Hartog","Corine Boon","Robert M. Verburg","Marcel A. Croon"],"y":2013,"c":"pub","j":"Journal of Management","v":"39","i":"6","p":"1637-1665","r":102,"l":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0149206312440118","lt":"pub","doi":"10.1177/0149206312440118"},{"t":"Work Engagement and Machiavellianism in the Ethical Leadership